10)Internal tables-
-Internal tables are temporary tables stored in application server memory and used to process multiple records in ABAP programs.
-An internal Excel sheet inside your program
-It stores multiple rows of data
eg.
DATA: lt_table TYPE TABLE OF string,

 their are 3 types of internal tables-
    1)standard internal table- It is an unsorted table with a unique key.
      -It allows duplicate entries and does not maintain any specific order.
      -access by index or by key.
      e.g DATA: lt_table TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF string WITH EMPTY KEY.

    2)sorted internal table- It is a sorted table with a unique key.
    It maintains the entries in a sorted order based on the key fields and does not allow duplicate entries
      - DATA: lt_table TYPE SORTED TABLE OF string WITH UNIQUE KEY table_line.

    e.g-REPORT z_sorted_demo.

    DATA lt_numbers TYPE SORTED TABLE OF i
                    WITH UNIQUE KEY table_line.
    INSERT 30 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.
    INSERT 10 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.
    INSERT 20 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.

    LOOP AT lt_numbers INTO DATA(lv_num).
      WRITE: / lv_num.
    ENDLOOP.

    3)hashed internal table- It is a hashed table with a unique key.
    It uses a hash algorithm to store and access entries based on the key fields, providing fast access times. It does not allow duplicate entries.
      e.g DATA: lt_table TYPE HASHED TABLE OF string WITH UNIQUE KEY table_line. 

    e.g-
    REPORT z_hashed_demo.

    DATA lt_numbers TYPE HASHED TABLE OF i
                    WITH UNIQUE KEY table_line.
    INSERT 100 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.
    INSERT 200 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.
    INSERT 300 INTO TABLE lt_numbers.

    READ TABLE lt_numbers WITH TABLE KEY table_line = 200
        INTO DATA(lv_num).

    IF sy-subrc = 0.
      WRITE 'Found'.
    ENDIF.

11)Work area-
-A work area is a single row of data that corresponds to the structure of an internal table.
-it is temporarily hold one row of an internal table.

eg.
DATA: it_table TYPE TABLE OF I,
     wa_table TYPE string.
APPEND 10 TO it_table.
APPEND 20 TO it_table.
APPEND 30 TO it_table.
LOOP AT it_table INTO wa_table.
  WRITE: / wa_table.

12)Internal table operations-
  1)append- adds a new row to the end of an internal table.
  eg.
  DATA: it_table TYPE TABLE OF I.
  APPEND 10 TO it_table.
  APPEND 20 TO it_table.
  LOOP AT it_table INTO DATA(lv_num).
    WRITE: / lv_num.
  ENDLOOP.
  2)insert- adds a new row to a specific position in an internal table.
  eg.
  DATA: it_table TYPE TABLE OF I.
  INSERT 10 INTO TABLE it_table INDEX 1.
  INSERT 20 INTO TABLE it_table INDEX 2.
  LOOP AT it_table INTO DATA(lv_num).
    WRITE: / lv_num.
  ENDLOOP.
  3)delete- removes a row from an internal table based on a specified condition.
  eg.
  DATA: it_table TYPE TABLE OF I.
  APPEND 10 TO it_table.
  APPEND 20 TO it_table.
  APPEND 30 TO it_table.
  DELETE it_table WHERE table_line = 20.
  LOOP AT it_table INTO DATA(lv_num).
    WRITE: / lv_num.  
  ENDLOOP.
  4)modify- updates a row in an internal table based on a specified condition.
  eg.
  DATA: it_table TYPE TABLE OF I.
  APPEND 10 TO it_table.
  APPEND 20 TO it_table.
  APPEND 30 TO it_table.
  MODIFY it_table FROM 25 WHERE table_line = 20.
  LOOP AT it_table INTO DATA(lv_num).
    WRITE: / lv_num.
  ENDLOOP.

13)Internal table statements-
  1)LOOP AT-
  LOOP AT is used to read and process rows of an internal table one by one.
  e.g-
  REPORT z_loop_demo.

  DATA lt_numbers TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF i.
  DATA lv_number TYPE i.

  APPEND 10 TO lt_numbers.
  APPEND 20 TO lt_numbers.
  APPEND 30 TO lt_numbers.

  LOOP AT lt_numbers INTO lv_number.
    WRITE: / lv_number.
  ENDLOOP.

  2)READ TABLE
  Used to search for a record in an internal table.

  e.g-
  DATA it_employee TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF string.
  DATA lv_emp TYPE string.

  APPEND 10 TO it_employee.
  APPEND 20 TO it_employee.

  READ TABLE it_employee INTO lv_emp WITH KEY table_line=20.

  IF sy-subrc = 0.
    WRITE 'found'.
  ELSE.
    WRITE 'not found'.

  ENDIF.    

  3)2️⃣ COLLECT (Very Important Concept ⭐)

  COLLECT is used to:
  Insert record
  If key already exists → Add numeric fields automatically

  e.g-
  REPORT z_collect_demo.

  TYPES: BEGIN OF ty_sales,
          product TYPE string,
          qty     TYPE i,
        END OF ty_sales.

  DATA: lt_sales TYPE STANDARD TABLE OF ty_sales,
        ls_sales TYPE ty_sales.

  ls_sales-product = 'Pen'.
  ls_sales-qty = 10.
  COLLECT ls_sales INTO lt_sales.

  ls_sales-product = 'Pen'.
  ls_sales-qty = 5.
  COLLECT ls_sales INTO lt_sales.

  LOOP AT lt_sales INTO ls_sales.
    WRITE: / ls_sales-product, ls_sales-qty.
  ENDLOOP.

  ouput-
  Pen  10
  {Product = 'Pen' already exists
  qty is numeric
  10 + 5 = 15}
  Pen  15

