14)Open SQl:
  1)select single:
  used to fetch one record from database.
  e.g
  SELECT SINGLE name 
  FROM zstudent 
  WHERE roll =1 INTO @DATA(lv_name).

  2)select into table:
  used to fetch multiple records into internal table.
  e.g
  SELECT * FROM zstudent INTO TABLE @DATA(it_student).

  3)WHERE clause:
  used to filter records
  e.g
  SELECT * FROM zstudent WHERE roll>1 INTO TABLE @DATA(it_student).

  4)INNER JOIN:
  return only matching records from both tables
  e.g
  SELECT a~roll,a~name,b~marks
  FROM zstudent AS a INNER JOIN zmarks AS b ON a~roll = b~roll INTO TABLE @DATA(it_result).

  5)LEFT OUTER JOIN:
  return left table record matching from right table.
  e.g
  SELECT a~roll,a~name,b~marks
  FROM zstudent AS a LEFT OUTER JOIN zmarks AS b ON a~roll = b~roll INTO TABLE @DATA(it_result).

  6)INSERT:
  used to insert new record into database table.
  e.g
  DATA ls_student TYPE zstudent.
  ls_student-roll = 4.
  ls_student-name = 'Neha'.
  INSERT zstudent FROM ls_student.

  7)upadte:
  used to modify existing record in database table.
  e.g
  UPDATE zstudent SET name = 'Neha' WHERE roll = 4.

  8)delete:
  used to remove record from database table.
  e.g
  DELETE FROM zstudent WHERE roll = 4.

  9)Aggregate functions:
  used to perform calculations on a set of values and return a single value.
    1)sum- used to calculate total sum of a numeric field.
    e.g
    SELECT SUM(marks) FROM zmarks INTO @DATA(lv_total_marks).
    2)avg- used to calculate average value of a numeric field.
    e.g
    SELECT AVG(marks) FROM zmarks INTO @DATA(lv_avg_marks).
    3)count- used to count number of records.
    e.g
    SELECT COUNT(*) FROM zstudent INTO @DATA(lv_total_students).
    4)max- used to find maximum value of a numeric field.
    e.g
    SELECT MAX(marks) FROM zmarks INTO @DATA(lv_max_marks).
    5)min- used to find minimum value of a numeric field.
    e.g
    SELECT MIN(marks) FROM zmarks INTO @DATA(lv_min_marks).

  10)FOR ALL ENTRIES:  
  Used to fetch records based on values from internal table.
  e.g
  SELECT *
    FROM zmarks
    INTO TABLE @DATA(lt_marks)
    FOR ALL ENTRIES IN @lt_students
    WHERE roll = @lt_students-roll.

  11)GROUP BY:
  Used to group records based on specified fields.
  Used aggregate functions to perform calculations on each group.
  e.g
  SELECT roll,SUM( marks ) AS total_marks
    FROM zmarks
    GROUP BY roll
    INTO TABLE @DATA(lt_result).

  12)HAVING:
  Used to filter groups based on specified conditions.
  e.g
  SELECT roll,SUM( marks ) AS total_marks
    FROM zmarks
    GROUP BY roll
    HAVING SUM( marks ) > 50
    INTO TABLE @DATA(lt_result).

